tions, could cause the stock price to decline.", "citations": ["TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0041"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "The fiscal 2025 10-K says Tesla must maintain credibility and confidence among investors and others in its long-term financial viability and business prospects.", "citations": ["TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0015"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "The fiscal 2025 10-K reports 3,752,431,984 shares of common stock outstanding as of January 23, 2026, with no statement about whether to buy them.", "citations": ["TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__unknown__0007"], "unverified": false}]}], "comparison_table": null, "citations": [{"chunk_id": "TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0041", "claim": "Musk share sales could lower stock price", "quote": "Any such sales could cause the price of our common stock to decline."}, {"chunk_id": "TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0015", "claim": "Need to maintain credibility and confidence", "quote": "we must maintain credibility and confidence among customers, suppliers, analysts, investors, ratings agencies and other parties"}, {"chunk_id": "TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__unknown__0007", "claim": "Shares outstanding as of January 23, 2026", "quote": "there were 3,752,431,984 shares of the registrant's common stock outstanding"}], "coverage": {"companies_used": [{"ticker": "TSLA", "forms": ["10-K"], "fiscal_periods": ["fiscal 2025, ended December 31, 2025"]}], "companies_missing": [], "data_as_of": "Latest filing: fiscal 2025 10-K, ended December 31, 2025, filed 2026-01-29"}, "gaps": ["SEC filings do not recommend buying or selling shares; the question asks for a recommendation the filings cannot provide.", "Keel does not give investment advice, price targets, or recommendations.", "Stock prices, valuation, and market events after the latest filing are not in the context.", "The filing does not rank its risks, so no severity ordering is given."], "confidence": "high", "confidence_reason": "The context contains no pur